INSTALL - snd-usb-mytek

1. Firmware: put the three Mytek firmware files into /lib/firmware/mytek,
   see FIRMWARE.

2. Build and install the module with DKMS (recommended: it is rebuilt
   automatically on every kernel update):

       sudo apt install dkms build-essential linux-headers-$(uname -r)
       sudo ./scripts/dkms-install.sh            # install / upgrade
       sudo ./scripts/dkms-install.sh --remove   # uninstall

   Tested on Ubuntu. Other distributions need the same packages, e.g.
   Fedora: sudo dnf install dkms gcc make kernel-devel-$(uname -r)
   Arch:   sudo pacman -S dkms base-devel linux-headers

   With Secure Boot the module must be signed with a key enrolled in MOK;
   see "Secure Boot" in README.md.

   Without DKMS (only for the running kernel, repeat after kernel updates):

       make
       sudo make install          # sudo make uninstall to remove

3. Switch the Mytek to its USB2 input and connect it. The module loads
   automatically and uploads the firmware; then

       aplay -l

   lists "card N: USB2 [Mytek Stereo192-DSD USB2], device 0: MytekUSB2".
   If it does not appear, see ISSUES.
